# Plan: customer satisfaction rating

Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved, Mai Do, 2026-01-12). Written 2026-10-07; nothing built.
Baseline: `node --test` on `7b9b2be` gives 7 pass, 0 fail.

## Goal

Customers rate a resolved ticket 1 to 5 once; a score of 1 or 2 emails the owner; a nightly job summarises each agent's last seven days; `assignee_id` becomes `owner_id`.

## Read this first: the spec conflicts with two facts in the repo

1. **Requirement 6 breaks finance.** `src/jobs/export-tickets.js:20-21` exports the stored fields, and finance's reader (deployed on its own schedule, not in this repo) reads `assignee_id`. The last acceptance criterion ("called `owner_id` wherever it was `assignee_id`") and finance's file cannot both hold on day one. Plan: export both names until a stated expiry (D1).
2. **Production is Postgres, outside this repo** (`README.md`). The rename and the new columns are migrations this repo cannot ship (D2).

## Phases

| # | Phase | Class | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Rename `assignee_id` to `owner_id`](phase-01-rename-owner.md) | COUNCIL (schema, external contract) | planned |
| 2 | [Store and portal: rate a ticket](phase-02-rate-ticket.md) | COUNCIL (schema) + hot path (tenant scoping) | planned |
| 3 | [Email the owner on a low score](phase-03-low-score-email.md) | ACT | planned |
| 4 | [Weekly summary job](phase-04-weekly-summary.md) | ACT, one COUNCIL point (new table) | planned |

Order: 1, then 2, 3, 4. Phase 1 goes first so later code never names `assignee_id`. Phases 1 and 2 each ship alone.

## Decisions

Full list with reasons: [decisions.md](decisions.md). I worked from my recommendations. Cheapest to get wrong, so confirm first:

| # | Question | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|
| D1 | Rename vs finance's export | Export writes `owner_id` and a `TEMPORARY` `assignee_id` copy, expiry 2026-12-15 |
| D2 | Who runs the Postgres migration | DB owner, expand then contract; the plan writes the request, not the SQL run |
